# Losses

Add losses by mirroring an existing neighbor in the same file (e.g. `DiceLoss` in `monai/losses/dice.py`). Load only that neighbor — do not read the whole package.

## Class

- Subclass `torch.nn.modules.loss._Loss` (or an existing loss to extend it, e.g. `LogCoshDiceLoss(DiceLoss)`).
- `__init__` stores params and calls `super().__init__(reduction=LossReduction(reduction).value)` when subclassing `_Loss` directly; validate mutually-exclusive flags early with `ValueError`.
- `forward(self, input: torch.Tensor, target: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor`; document shapes `BNH[WD]`.
- Honor `reduction` (`"mean"`, `"sum"`, `"none"`).

## Register (miss it and imports break)

- Add the class name to the correct `from .<module> import (...)` block in `monai/losses/__init__.py`, in case-insensitive alphabetical order. There is **no** per-file `__all__`.

## Always

- Apache header; `from __future__ import annotations`; Google-style docstrings; American English.
- Do not use APIs listed in `docs/cursor-kit/monai-refs/deprecations.md`.

Full skeleton + named neighbor: `docs/cursor-kit/monai-refs/losses.md`.

**Source of truth:** `monai/losses/dice.py`, `monai/losses/__init__.py`, `docs/cursor-kit/monai-refs/losses.md`
